{
  "requirement": "The enabled Habeas Symposium plugin MUST request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI and use that installation as its session-start hook command, so the CLI is available when the hook advises an agent to run `habeas setup`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text says the Symposium plugin MUST request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI and use that installation as its session-start hook command. Both parts are structural, because they are declared in Symposium plugin metadata. Dropping either one would break the clause even if the rest of the plugin behaved the same.\n\nThe `Cargo.toml` roots carry both parts:\n- **Installation:** `Cargo.toml#table[package.metadata.symposium.installations]` has `name = \"habeas\"` (`pair[name]`), `source = \"cargo\"` (`pair[source]`), `crate = \"habeas\"` (`pair[crate]`) and `global = true` (`pair[global]`). Together these request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` crate. Changing the source or setting global to false would violate the clause.\n- **Hook command:** `Cargo.toml#table[package.metadata.symposium.hooks]` has `command = \"habeas\"` (`pair[command]`). This names the installation as the hook command. It sits in the entry named `habeas-setup-check` (`pair[name]`), which also sets the SessionStart event and the symposium format.\n\nThe hook name is a label and is not constrained by the text. Marking it with the requirement is harmless, because it identifies the hook entry that carries the command.\n\nThe event and format pairs belong to `requirements.integration.symposium_setup_hook` and are marked for that requirement. No other structural obligation, such as a library, signature or type, is stated, and no further implementation root is needed.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has two observable obligations. First, the plugin must request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI. Second, the session-start hook command must be that installed CLI.\n\n`tests/repository.rs#fn[symposium_plugin_installs_the_cli_globally_for_its_session_start_hook]` carries the `{test}` reference and covers both obligations.\n\n- **Installation request.** It parses `Cargo.toml` and asserts that `package.metadata.symposium.installations` has exactly one entry. It asserts `source == \"cargo\"`, `crate == \"habeas\"`, `executable == \"habeas\"` and `global == true`.\n- **Hook command.** It asserts that `hooks` has exactly one entry with `event == \"SessionStart\"`. It asserts that the hook `command` equals the installation's `executable`, so the hook uses the installed CLI. It also asserts that `args` are `[\"hook\", \"session-start\"]`, which goes beyond what this requirement states.\n\nThe assertions are strict equality checks. A non-global install, a different source or crate, a different hook command, or a hook that does not match the installation would each fail the test.\n\nThe requirement's wording \"enabled plugin\" and \"advises an agent to run `habeas setup`\" describes the hook's purpose. It adds no separate testable condition for this requirement. The advice itself belongs to `requirements.integration.symposium_setup_hook`, a separate requirement.\n\nI found no gaps.",
  "references": "a6c4f0e64a68bbc6401b55bf90de985d33452cf5264c17d707356e164d24e9dc",
