        "rationale": "The requirement has two observable obligations. First, the plugin must request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI. Second, the session-start hook command must be that installed CLI.\n\n`tests/repository.rs#fn[symposium_plugin_installs_the_cli_globally_for_its_session_start_hook]` carries the `{test}` reference and covers both obligations.\n\n- **Installation request.** It parses `Cargo.toml` and asserts that `package.metadata.symposium.installations` has exactly one entry. It asserts `source == \"cargo\"`, `crate == \"habeas\"`, `executable == \"habeas\"` and `global == true`.\n- **Hook command.** It asserts that `hooks` has exactly one entry with `event == \"SessionStart\"`. It asserts that the hook `command` equals the installation's `executable`, so the hook uses the installed CLI. It also asserts that `args` are `[\"hook\", \"session-start\"]`, which goes beyond what this requirement states.\n\nThe assertions are strict equality checks. A non-global install, a different source or crate, a different hook command, or a hook that does not match the installation would each fail the test.\n\nThe requirement's wording \"enabled plugin\" and \"advises an agent to run `habeas setup`\" describes the hook's purpose. It adds no separate testable condition for this requirement. The advice itself belongs to `requirements.integration.symposium_setup_hook`, a separate requirement.\n\nI found no gaps."
